78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/coding-agents.md:10:For optional help from your coding agent, [Set it up for me](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/setup-with-agent.md) has prompts for an existing LiteLLM deployment, standalone Lens, and external ClickHouse. The agent should inspect the installed version before applying this guide
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment.md:13:Prefer your coding agent to configure the project? [Set it up for me](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/setup-with-agent.md) has optional copyable prompts for standalone Lens, an existing LiteLLM deployment, and external ClickHouse. Keep the manual path below if you prefer to run the commands yourself
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment.md:19:For an existing Lens deployment, use the [metadata migration guide](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/migration.md) before handing its writers to the independent service. Lens can keep its existing ClickHouse trace data; PostgreSQL is only an import source for Lens metadata. LiteLLM keeps its own gateway database.
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/configuration.md:9:For optional help from your coding agent, [Set it up for me](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/setup-with-agent.md) has prompts for an existing LiteLLM deployment, standalone Lens, and external ClickHouse. The agent should inspect the installed version before applying this guide
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/development.md:9:For optional help from your coding agent, [Set it up for me](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/setup-with-agent.md) has prompts for an existing LiteLLM deployment, standalone Lens, and external ClickHouse. The agent should inspect the installed version before applying this guide
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/docker-compose.md:9:For optional help from your coding agent, [Set it up for me](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/setup-with-agent.md) has prompts for an existing LiteLLM deployment, standalone Lens, and external ClickHouse. The agent should inspect the installed version before applying this guide
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/docker.md:9:For optional help from your coding agent, [Set it up for me](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/setup-with-agent.md) has prompts for an existing LiteLLM deployment, standalone Lens, and external ClickHouse. The agent should inspect the installed version before applying this guide
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/kubernetes.md:9:For optional help from your coding agent, [Set it up for me](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/setup-with-agent.md) has prompts for an existing LiteLLM deployment, standalone Lens, and external ClickHouse. The agent should inspect the installed version before applying this guide
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/local.md:13:For optional help from your coding agent, copy the [standalone setup prompt](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/setup-with-agent.md#start-standalone-lens). It includes connecting this project's agent and verifying its first trace
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/local.md:18:git clone https://github.com/BerriAI/lens.git
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/local.md:31:The local trace endpoint is `http://localhost:4318/v1/traces`. That address works for an agent running on the same host. Agents in another container or on another machine need a reachable Lens address; see [deployment configuration](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/deploy/lens/README.md#configure-a-deployment).
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/local.md:37:Once traces arrive, [configure an analysis model](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/analysis.md), then create an investigation. You can connect Lens directly to a supported provider or use an existing LiteLLM model endpoint.
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/local.md:45:Run `./deploy/lens/start` to start them again. Retain `deploy/lens/.env` and the ClickHouse volume. Adding `--volumes` to `down` deletes stored Lens data. For persistence, troubleshooting and backups, use the [Lens deployment guide](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/deploy/lens/README.md).
78c66d034dafecab8a8d7efa41591cedd8a23c84:docs/proxy/lens/deployment/server.md:9:For optional help from your coding agent, [Set it up for me](https://github.com/BerriAI/lens/blob/main/docs/setup-with-agent.md) has prompts for an existing LiteLLM deployment, standalone Lens, and external ClickHouse. The agent should inspect the installed version before applying this guide
